  "fidelityReview": {
    "target": "medium-fi",
    "status": "passed",
    "inputHash": "sha256:399f8f70f2802235d24fff77b8c27cda335061698344bc45f8870f9694f46629",
    "notes": "The principal historic exterior retains the three projecting waterfront pavilions and two inset bays, the rusticated basement, two arched window stories, shallow closed hipped roofs, and both southwest stair flights. The granite-facing strip runs only along the mapped historic court frontage. The 3.5 m court level, offshore bed correction and stair risers are visual estimates from the ordinary exterior photos and standard map and terrain inputs. The site grade blends into the raw hill behind the palace. This is the principal historic exterior with its closed roofs, southwest entrance and both stair flights. A short granite-faced seawall follows the mapped line along the historic court. The independent hotel, pool, gardens, gate and remaining quay retain their map geometry. Unseen facade details and decorative trim are original medium-fi interpretations. Ornament, letters and interiors are outside the modeled scope."
  },
